# Build context trim for `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .` (root context, whole tree).
#
# docker/Dockerfile deliberately does `COPY . .` rather than naming pom.xml and src/: a file list
# has to be edited every time the repo gains top-level content the build needs, and forgetting is
# silent. This file is what makes that affordable — it drops everything the build does not read, so
# adding a top-level entry stays free and no stale output leaks in.
.git
.gitignore

# Maven / Quarkus build output — regenerated inside the build stage, and a stale target/ here would
# risk shadowing what the stage compiles.
target
target-ide

# Local env / IDE cruft
.env
.idea
.vscode
.sdkmanrc

# Docs and the docker/ dir itself: nothing in the build reads them, and keeping them out means
# editing this Dockerfile or the README does not bust the `COPY . .` layer.
*.md
docker
# …except the two things the image itself carries from it: the entrypoint and the init helper's Go
# source (the `wireguard` stage builds it). Editing either does bust the build stage's `COPY . .`,
# which is the price of keeping that COPY a whole-tree one.
!docker/entrypoint.sh
!docker/edge-init
